olor":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":15,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1856,1024],"size":[806,136],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"ControlNet model + type","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## ControlNet model + type\n\n**Load ControlNet Model** → CONTROL_NET. Your file is a **Union** model (one file, many control types), so **Set Union ControlNet Type** tells it which: here *canny*."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## ControlNet model + type\n\n**Load ControlNet Model** → CONTROL_NET. Your file is a **Union** model (one file, many control types), so **Set Union ControlNet Type** tells it which: here *canny*."},"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":16,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1856,1220],"size":[806,231],"flags":{},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Apply ControlNet + Try this","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Apply ControlNet + Try this\n\nInputs: positive + negative CONDITIONING, CONTROL_NET, the control IMAGE (+ VAE). Outputs: **modified** positive + negative → KSampler.\n- **strength** 0.4-0.9 · **end_percent** < 1 lets the model finish details freely.\n\n**Try this:** strength 0.3 vs 1.0 · prompt *a hazmat-suited station worker* / *a crew member overgrown with dark fungus* · use `side.png` as reference, or a room like `corridor_day.png` (Empty Latent 1344×768) to keep a room's layout but redesign it. This is how you keep character poses consistent across game art."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Apply ControlNet + Try this\n\nInputs: positive + negative CONDITIONING, CONTROL_NET, the control IMAGE (+ VAE). Outputs: **modified** positive + negative → KSampler.\n- **strength** 0.4-0.9 · **end_percent** < 1 lets the model finish details freely.\n\n**Try this:** strength 0.3 vs 1.0 · prompt *a hazmat-suited station worker* / *a crew member overgrown with dark fungus* · use `side.png` as reference, or a room like `corridor_day.png` (Empty Latent 1344×768) to keep a room's layout but redesign it. This is how you keep character poses consistent across game art."},"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":17,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-640,40],"size":[560,497],"flags":{},"order":7,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"11 · ControlNet: keep the pose, change everything else","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## 11 · ControlNet: keep the pose, change everything else\n\n**ControlNet** forces the new image to follow the **structure** of a reference (edges, depth, pose) while the prompt decides the content.\n\nPipeline: reference → **preprocessor** (Canny edges) → **Apply ControlNet** modifies the prompts' CONDITIONING → KSampler.\n\n### How to use every tutorial\n1. Read this box, then the boxes **below** the nodes (left → right).\n2. Click **Run** (or **Ctrl+Enter**). The result appears in the Save/Preview node and the queue panel.\n3. Do the **Try this** experiments and Run again - learning = changing one thing at a time.\n\n**Reading the graph:** coloured frames run **left → right**: 1 MODELS → 2 INPUTS → 3 PROMPTS → 4 GENERATE → 5 OUTPUT. Wires only turn in the gaps between columns; the **dots** on wires are *reroutes* (drag one to re-route a wire). Follow a wire by its colour = its data type.\n\n**Canvas tips:** drag empty space to pan · scroll to zoom · **.** fits everything · double-click empty canvas to **search & add a node** · click a node + **Ctrl+B** bypasses it · **Ctrl+Z** undo."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## 11 · ControlNet: keep the pose, change everything else\n\n**ControlNet** forces the new image to follow the **structure** of a reference (edges, depth, pose) while the prompt decides the content.\n\nPipeline: reference → **preprocessor** (Canny edges) → **Apply ControlNet** modifies the prompts' CONDITIONING → KSampler.\n\n### How to use every tutorial\n1. Read this box, then the boxes **below** the nodes (left → right).\n2. Click **Run** (or **Ctrl+Enter**). The result appears in the Save/Preview node and the queue panel.\n3. Do the **Try this** experiments and Run again - learning = changing one thing at a time.\n\n**Reading the graph:** coloured frames run **left → right**: 1 MODELS → 2 INPUTS → 3 PROMPTS → 4 GENERATE → 5 OUTPUT. Wires only turn in the gaps between columns; the **dots** on wires are *reroutes* (drag one to re-route a wire). Follow a wire by its colour = its data type.\n\n**Canvas tips:** drag empty space to pan · scroll to zoom · **.** fits everything · double-click empty canvas to **search & add a node** · click a node + **Ctrl+B** bypasses it · **Ctrl+Z** undo."},"color":"#223","bgcolor":"#335"}],"links":[[18,2,0,3,0,"IMAGE"],[19,3,0,4,0,"IMAGE"],[20,5,0,6,0,"CONTROL_NET"],[21,1,1,7,0,"CLIP"],[22,1,1,8,0,"CLIP"],[23,7,0,9,0,"CONDITIONING"],[24,8,0,9,1,"CONDITIONING"],[25,6,0,9,2,"CONTROL_NET"],[26,3,0,9,3,"IMAGE"],[27,1,2,9,4,"VAE"],[28,1,0,11,0,"MODEL"],[29,9,0,11,1,"CONDITIONING"],[30,9,1,11,2,"CONDITIONING"],[31,10,0,11,3,"LATENT"],[32,11,0,12,0,"LATENT"],[33,1,2,12,1,"VAE"],[34,12,0,13,0,"IMAGE"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"1 · MODELS","bounding":[0,0,368,434],"color":"#A88","flags":{}},{"id":2,"title":"2 · INPUTS","bounding":[532,0,1108,786],"color":"#b58b2a","flags":{}},{"id":3,"title":"3 · PROMPTS & CONDITIONING","bounding":[1822,0,874,1515],"color":"#88A","flags":{}},{"id":4,"title":"4 · GENERATE","bounding":[2806,0,774,1124],"color":"#8A8","flags":{}},{"id":5,"title":"5 · OUTPUT","bounding":[3672,0,738,838],"color":"#3f789e","flags":{}}],"config":{},"extra":{"ds":{"scale":0.9,"offset":[416,110]},"linkExtensions":[{"id":20,"parentId":1},{"id":22,"parentId":5},{"id":24,"parentId":9},{"id":25,"parentId":11},{"id":26,"parentId":13},{"id":27,"parentId":19},{"id":28,"parentId":25},{"id":29,"parentId":29},{"id":30,"parentId":33},{"id":31,"parentId":37},{"id":33,"parentId":39}],"reroutes":[{"id":1,"parentId":2,"pos":[1704,828],"linkIds":[20]},{"id":2,"parentId":3,"pos":[1704,352],"linkIds":[20]},{"id":3,"parentId":4,"pos":[414,352],"linkIds":[20]},{"id":4,"pos":[414,316],"linkIds"